Implement eval/plan008_metrics.py + eval/tests/test_plan008_metrics.py (CPU only, stdlib only, counts only, never print task text).

READ FIRST: eval/plans/008.md (Metrics section + Addendum D71.2 + Addendum D72.2 = the binding definitions), eval/plan007_arm1_summary.py (input layout, PARTS, assert_paired, identical_runs, how per-task trace runs/<run>/runs/<instance_id>/trace.json is read: d['entries'], each entry has 'type' (tool_call/tool_result/thinking/...), 'author', 'tool', 'args'), bundles/31b/v010/sub_agents/submit_gate.yaml (gate output format: 'GATE call=<n> kept_files=<c>' then 'VERDICT=SUBMIT reason=changes|forced|check_error' or 'VERDICT=EDIT_FIRST'; gate replies 'SUBMITTED' / 'NOT SUBMITTED: ...' / 'SUBMIT FAILED: ...'). Inspect one real arm-1 trace (runs/31b-v009-p7a1-main/runs/*/trace.json) to learn exactly how tool_call and tool results/responses are linked and how agent_tool (code_analyzer_agent) nested entries appear (author field).

FUNCTIONS (importable, each unit-tested on synthetic in-memory traces):
1. root_tool_calls(entries, root='swe_baseline_agent'): tool_call entries with author == root, in order, each paired with its response text (whatever field links call->result in the real trace format).
2. identical_runs_root(entries): same as plan007_arm1_summary.identical_runs but on root_tool_calls only (D72.2 ROOT filter). Returns max_run, runs_ge3, runs_ge5, repeated_calls.
3. successful_submit_index(entries): index in root_tool_calls of the FIRST root submit_patch call that succeeded: arm 1 = its response contains a patch_size field and no error status; arm 2 (gate) = the gate's final reply text for that call starts with 'SUBMITTED' (and not 'SUBMIT FAILED'). None if no success.
4. submitted_without_test(entries): True iff successful_submit_index is not None and no root run_command before it has a command arg matching re r'\bpytest\b|-m\s+unittest\b|\btox\b'. None-success rows return None (reported as count_no_successful_submit).
5. gate_descriptives(entries): per row: gate_calls (root submit_patch calls), bounces (gate reply starts 'NOT SUBMITTED'), forced (a gate-authored run_command response contains 'reason=forced'), check_error ('reason=check_error'), submit_failed (reply starts 'SUBMIT FAILED'), bounce_no_followup (a bounce with no later root tool_call), gate_run_cmds (list of the gate-authored run_command command strings, for smoke (i) byte-identity vs the YAML step-1 line). Gate-authored = author == 'submit_patch'. If NO entry has author 'submit_patch' but root submit_patch calls exist with gate-style replies, set gate_internal_visible=False.
6. untracked_only(patch_text): True iff patch non-empty and every 'diff --git' section has a 'new file mode' line.
7. smoke_check(row, entries, gate_yaml_path): returns dict of criteria i..v per eval/plans/008.md D71.2 (+ D72.2 last bullet) with PASS/FAIL/UNVERIFIABLE and a reason string; (iv) uses the row's agent clock field the same way plan007 uses agent_timing (if not derivable, UNVERIFIABLE). (ii) compares row verified_patch_bytes (or the field plan007 uses for patch size) to patch_size in the inner submit_patch response.

CLI: python3 eval/plan008_metrics.py base OUT_JSON  -> computes, for ARM 1 (same PARTS/inputs as plan007_arm1_summary.py, reuse its loaders by import), per-row and totals of: mechanism2 (rows with root max_run>=5; MUST equal 17 -> assert), submitted_without_test count + count_no_successful_submit, mechanism1 empty count (reuse plan007's empty definition; must equal 12 -> assert). Output schema-headed JSON (_schema with definitions text, script sha256, input shas). Also: python3 eval/plan008_metrics.py smoke RUN_DIR OUT_JSON (rows from RUN_DIR/timing.jsonl, traces RUN_DIR/runs/<id>/trace.json, gate yaml bundles/31b/v010/sub_agents/submit_gate.yaml) -> smoke verdict JSON with per-task criteria and overall PASS only if all criteria PASS in every task.

TESTS (pytest, synthetic traces): root filter: 5 identical root submit_patch calls interleaved with gate-authored run_command entries -> max_run 5 (and the unfiltered plan007 function gives 1); successful-submit boundary: bounce, edit, pytest run, successful submit -> submitted_without_test False; pytest only after a bounce but before success -> False; no test before success -> True; never succeeds -> None; gate descriptives counts on a synthetic 2-bounce-then-forced trace; untracked_only cases; smoke_check PASS case and FAIL cases for each criterion (i)-(v). Plus one test that runs the base CLI on the real arm-1 inputs if runs/31b-v009-p7a1-main exists (skip otherwise) and asserts mechanism2==17 and empty==12.

